From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UnsleptArch <sirinotomer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:35:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] 9520: PyGhidra: fix extension.properties parsing of values
 containing '='

ExtensionDetails.from_file split each line on every '=', so it raised
ValueError on any properties file whose value contains an '=', and on
blank or comment lines.

PyGhidra writes this file itself (_install_plugin does
ext.write_text(str(details))) and reads it back in _uninstall_old_plugin,
so a plugin whose description contains an '=' produced a file PyGhidra
could not parse. The read is wrapped in a bare except that only logs, so
the outdated extension is silently left installed instead.

str.partition keeps the first '=' as the separator and lets lines without
one be skipped, matching what ApplicationInfo.from_file already does.
---
 .../src/main/py/src/pyghidra/version.py       |  4 +-
 .../src/main/py/tests/test_version.py         | 57 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/tests/test_version.py

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/src/pyghidra/version.py b/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/src/pyghidra/version.py
index 0f70b751cf..4c013a57e2 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/src/pyghidra/version.py
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/src/pyghidra/version.py
@@ -79,8 +79,8 @@ class ExtensionDetails:
         lines = ext_path.read_text().splitlines()
         kwargs = {
             key: cast(key, value)
-            for key, value in map(lambda l: l.split("="), lines)
-            if key in valid_fields
+            for key, sep, value in map(lambda l: l.partition("="), lines)
+            if sep and key in valid_fields
         }
         return cls(**kwargs)
 
diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/tests/test_version.py b/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/tests/test_version.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..d3a0fbe773
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/PyGhidra/src/main/py/tests/test_version.py
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
